WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.321
Each block contains one warp of thirty-two

00:00:03.321 --> 00:00:04.934
threads. With alternating signs,

00:00:04.934 --> 00:00:06.949
neighboring lanes take different paths

00:00:06.949 --> 00:00:08.158
through the kernel.

00:00:12.658 --> 00:00:15.033
Look at block zero. How many lanes will

00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:16.221
take the negative path?

00:00:24.722 --> 00:00:27.174
Sixteen lanes take the negative path and

00:00:27.174 --> 00:00:29.626
sixteen take the other path. Both warps

00:00:29.626 --> 00:00:31.378
contain a mixture of paths.

00:00:35.878 --> 00:00:38.756
In the grouped case, the first warp has

00:00:38.756 --> 00:00:41.274
only negative inputs and the second has

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:43.432
only positive inputs. Timing depends on

00:00:43.432 --> 00:00:45.950
the compiled instructions and work on each

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:46.310
path.
